hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16248","He said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Ubayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: And I heard it from Uqbah, but I retain the hadith of Ubayd better. He said: I married, then a black woman came to us and said: I have suckled you both. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married the woman so-and-so daughter of so-and-so, then a black woman came to us and said: I have suckled you both, and she is a disbeliever. So he turned away from me. Then I came to him from before his face and said: She is lying. He said to me: How about it, when she has claimed that she suckled you both? Leave her."
"16249","He said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ismail, meaning Ibn Umayyah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Uqbah ibn al-Harith: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, then a black woman came, meaning: then she mentioned that she had suckled you both. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stood before him and spoke to him, but he turned away from me. Then I stood on his right and he turned away from me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, she is only a black woman. He said: How so, when it has been said?"
"16250","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Nuayman after he had drunk wine, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those in the house and they beat him with hands and palm stalks and sandals. He said: And I was among those who beat him."
"16251","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: I prayed Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he gave the salam he rose quickly and entered upon one of his wives, then came out, and he saw what was on the faces of the people of their wonder and it was obscure to him. He said: I remembered while in prayer some gold with us, and I disliked that evening come or it spend the night with us, so I ordered it to be distributed."
"16252","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away when he had prayed Asr, then he mentioned its meaning."
"16253","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, or I heard it from him, that he married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab, then a black woman came and said: I have suckled you both. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he turned away from me. Then I moved aside and mentioned it to him, so he said: How so, when she has claimed that she has suckled you both? So he forbade him from her."
"16254","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed us that Uqbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir informed him, or he heard it from him if he did not particularly address it to him, that he married the daughter of Abu Ihab, then a black slave girl said: I have suckled you both. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, but he turned away from me. Then I came and mentioned it to him, so he said: How so, when she has claimed that she has suckled you both? So he forbade him from her."
"16255","He said: Sulayman ibn Harb and Affan narrated to us, they said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us; Affan said in his hadith, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Uqbah ibn al-Harith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Nuayman, or Ibn al-Nuayman, while drunk. He said: It was hard upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered those in the house to beat him, so they beat him. Affan said in his hadith: It caused the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) severe distress. Uqbah said: And I was among those who beat him."
